From: BRL-CAD developers <devs@brlcad.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Add CLIPPER2_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS option to produce a static archive alongside the shared library

Consumers that link their own code statically (e.g. BRL-CAD's static
library targets, or any framework that avoids runtime shared-library
dependencies) need a static Clipper2 archive so they can link without
carrying libClipper2.so as a runtime dependency.

Clipper2 already sets CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON globally, so
the object files produced for the shared library are already PIC-clean.
This patch adds an opt-in option CLIPPER2_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS that:

 - Builds a second target, Clipper2_static, from the same source list
   using add_library(... STATIC ...) immediately after the shared target
   is defined.
 - Sets OUTPUT_NAME Clipper2 (so the archive is libClipper2.a on disk,
   avoiding a confusingly named libClipper2_static.a).
 - Sets EXPORT_NAME Clipper2-static so the installed CMake target is
   Clipper2::Clipper2-static, following the conventional -static suffix
   naming used by other BRL-CAD bundled deps (e.g. manifold::manifold-static).
 - Propagates the same PUBLIC compile definitions (CLIPPER2_MAX_DECIMAL_PRECISION,
   CLIPPER2_HI_PRECISION) and include directories as the shared target.
 - Adds the static target to the Clipper2Targets export set so that
   Clipper2Config.cmake exposes it to consumers automatically.

Default is OFF so no existing workflow is changed.

A consumer that does:

  target_link_libraries(myapp PRIVATE Clipper2::Clipper2-static)

gets the full static Clipper2 archive linked in without needing to carry
libClipper2.so at runtime.  The shared Clipper2::Clipper2 target is
unchanged and continues to work as before.

Applies to: AngusJohnson/Clipper2, tag 1.5.2 (CPP/CMakeLists.txt)
--- a/CPP/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CPP/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ set(CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON)
 option(CLIPPER2_UTILS "Build utilities" OFF)
 option(CLIPPER2_EXAMPLES "Build examples" OFF)
 option(CLIPPER2_TESTS "Build tests" OFF)
 option(CLIPPER2_USINGZ "Build Z coordinate version" FALSE)
+option(CLIPPER2_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS "Also build a static library (Clipper2-static) alongside the shared library" OFF)
 
 if(MSVC)
   set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)

@@ -56,6 +57,42 @@ install(TARGETS Clipper2 EXPORT Clipper2Targets
   PUBLIC_HEADER DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/clipper2
   INCLUDES      DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}
 )
+
+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Optional static library target
+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+if(CLIPPER2_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS)
+  add_library(Clipper2_static STATIC ${CLIPPER2_INC} ${CLIPPER2_SRC})
+
+  set_target_properties(Clipper2_static PROPERTIES
+    OUTPUT_NAME  Clipper2
+    EXPORT_NAME  Clipper2-static
+  )
+
+  target_compile_definitions(Clipper2_static PUBLIC
+    CLIPPER2_MAX_DECIMAL_PRECISION=8
+    $<$<BOOL:${CLIPPER2_USINGZ}>:CLIPPER2_HI_PRECISION>
+  )
+
+  target_include_directories(Clipper2_static
+    PUBLIC
+      $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include>
+      $<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}>
+  )
+
+  target_link_libraries(Clipper2_static PUBLIC $<$<NOT:$<BOOL:${WIN32}>>:m>)
+
+  install(TARGETS Clipper2_static EXPORT Clipper2Targets
+    ARCHIVE  DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}
+    INCLUDES DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}
+  )
+endif()
+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+
 install(EXPORT Clipper2Targets
   NAMESPACE Clipper2::
   FILE Clipper2Targets.cmake
